  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "The CVE Program identifies the **CVE List** (the official catalog of CVE Records) as what feeds NVD. That list is operated under the **CVE Program**, which is run by **The MITRE Corporation** (HSSEDI, a DHS FFRDC operated by MITRE), with sponsorship from CISA. NVD (NIST) then enriches those records; it does not originate them.\n\nRelevant sources:\n\n1. **CVE Program (cve.org) — Related Efforts** — “The CVE List feeds NVD,” which builds on CVE Records; CVE and NVD are separate programs. The CVE List was launched by The MITRE Corporation (1999); NVD by NIST (2005).  \n   https://www.cve.org/about/relatedefforts\n\n2. **CVE Program FAQs** — CVE is copyrighted/trademarked by The MITRE Corporation and sponsored by CISA; HSSEDI (MITRE) executes the CVE Program Secretariat and related roles. The CVE List feeds NVD.  \n   https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n3. **NVD — Vulnerability Status** — “Vulnerability records within the NVD dataset are sourced from the CVE List, which is maintained by the CVE Program, upstream of the NVD.”  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/vulnerability-status\n\n4. **NVD — CVEs and the NVD Process** — CVE is maintained by the MITRE Corporation and sponsored by DHS/CISA; IDs are assigned by MITRE and CNAs. CVEs published to the CVE List typically appear in NVD within about an hour; NVD then enriches them.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cve-process\n\n5. **NVD — CVE FAQs** — After publication to the official CVE List, NVD enriches each CVE (CVSS, CWE, CPE, reference tags). NVD does not control CVE descriptions or reference links.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/CVE-FAQs\n\n6. **NVD — CVE 4.0 to 5.0 transition** — “All vulnerability records within the NVD are currently derived from the CVE List.” Publication to that list is controlled by CNAs under CVE Program operations.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/news/cve-4-0-to-cve-5-0-transition\n\n7. **Official CVE List (GitHub, CVEProject/cvelistV5)** — Described as the official CVE List: a catalog of CVE Records identified by or reported to the CVE Program, updated from the CVE Services API.  \n   https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5\n\n8. **NVD — CNAs and CVE Counting** — Submissions go to MITRE’s CVE list; after assignment and publication, NVD analyzes and publishes them. Organizations that assign CVE IDs are CNAs.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cna-counting",
